<article class="env-definition" id="0165">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0165">Definition <span data-tag="0165">14.2.1</span>.</a> For any integer $n\geq 1$, and any $0\leq j \leq n$ we let <em>$\delta ^ n_ j : [n-1] \to [n]$</em> denote the injective order preserving map skipping $j$. For any integer $n\geq 0$, and any $0\leq j \leq n$ we denote <em>$\sigma ^ n_ j : [n + 1] \to [n]$</em> the surjective order preserving map with $(\sigma ^ n_ j)^{-1}(\{ j\} ) = \{ j, j + 1\} $. </p>
</article>